eager:
And there a seed, racked with heroic pain,
Thrust eager tentacles to sun and rain;
It climbed; it died; the old love conquered me

eagle:
Filling the air with its morning lay;
'Twas not an eagle bold and strong,
Borne on the tempest's wing along.

eagle's:
Cherries suit robins;
The eagle's golden breakfast
Strangles them.

eaglets:
Or may be slept too late;
With eaglets broidered on his cap,
And eaglets on his glove?
